1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,830
Between 2019 and 2022, a driver in Ho Chi
Minh City kept a notebook.

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:10,796
According to prosecutors, it recorded cash
he carried out of one bank, on his boss's

3
00:00:10,796 --> 00:00:11,293
orders.

4
00:00:11,843 --> 00:00:18,989
The total: 108 trillion dong. More than
four billion dollars. In cash.

5
00:00:19,989 --> 00:00:24,650
At the same bank, tens of thousands of
ordinary savers were being offered

6
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,459
something that sounded as safe as a
deposit.

7
00:00:27,459 --> 00:00:28,098
It wasn't.

8
00:00:28,348 --> 00:00:34,078
This is the story of Truong My Lan. A real
estate tycoon who, a court found, secretly

9
00:00:34,078 --> 00:00:38,528
controlled a major Vietnamese bank, and
used it as her own wallet.

10
00:00:40,028 --> 00:00:44,455
Ho Chi Minh City. Vietnam's biggest city
and its money capital.

11
00:00:44,455 --> 00:00:50,217
In the 1980s and 90s, as Vietnam opened
its economy, fortunes were made here fast.

12
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:55,802
Truong My Lan was born in Saigon in 1956,
into a family of Chinese descent.

13
00:00:55,802 --> 00:01:00,970
According to state media and international
reporting, she started out selling

14
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:06,005
cosmetics with her mother at a stall in
Ben Thanh Market, the city's oldest

15
00:01:06,005 --> 00:01:06,475
market.

16
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:10,658
In 1992, she founded a company called Van
Thinh Phat.

17
00:01:10,658 --> 00:01:16,280
Over the next thirty years, it grew into
one of the biggest property groups in the

18
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:16,828
country.

19
00:01:16,828 --> 00:01:21,764
Luxury hotels. Office towers. Shopping
malls in the heart of District 1.

20
00:01:22,314 --> 00:01:26,505
She married a Hong Kong businessman, and
kept a low public profile.

21
00:01:26,505 --> 00:01:31,383
To most Vietnamese, she was simply one
more name in a booming property market.

22
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:37,106
Her niece would later run the group as its
chief executive. Her husband stood beside

23
00:01:37,106 --> 00:01:40,689
her in business. It was, in many ways, a
family empire.

24
00:01:40,689 --> 00:01:44,078
But building towers takes enormous amounts
of money.

25
00:01:44,078 --> 00:01:47,661
And the cheapest money, if you can get it,
is a bank's.

26
00:01:48,861 --> 00:01:54,686
In late 2011, in a merger approved by the
central bank, three struggling lenders

27
00:01:54,686 --> 00:01:58,255
became one: Saigon Commercial Bank, known
as SCB.

28
00:01:58,255 --> 00:02:00,512
It was supposed to be a rescue.

29
00:02:00,512 --> 00:02:04,080
According to the court, it became
something else.

30
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:10,751
Vietnamese law limits how much of a bank
any one person can own. On paper, Lan held

31
00:02:10,751 --> 00:02:14,880
a small stake. State media put it at about
five percent.

32
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:21,001
But the Ho Chi Minh City court later found
that she was the real owner of more than

33
00:02:21,001 --> 00:02:23,139
91.5 percent of SCB's shares.

34
00:02:23,689 --> 00:02:28,484
How do you own nine-tenths of a bank while
appearing to own almost nothing?

35
00:02:28,484 --> 00:02:28,996
Proxies.

36
00:02:29,246 --> 00:02:34,003
According to investigators, relatives,
employees and associates held shares in

37
00:02:34,003 --> 00:02:39,187
their own names. The court said the people
holding more than 75 percent of the shares

38
00:02:39,187 --> 00:02:41,505
all admitted they were acting for her.

39
00:02:42,055 --> 00:02:44,462
And with the shares came the people.

40
00:02:44,462 --> 00:02:49,878
The court found that from 2012 she picked
the bank's key managers, set up special

41
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:54,425
units to handle lending and payouts, and
gave instructions directly.

42
00:02:54,425 --> 00:02:57,033
Officially, she was not on SCB's board.

43
00:02:57,283 --> 00:03:00,658
In practice, the court said, the bank
answered to her.

44
00:03:01,858 --> 00:03:06,956
So how do you move billions of dollars out
of a bank you secretly control, without

45
00:03:06,956 --> 00:03:07,951
anyone noticing?

46
00:03:07,951 --> 00:03:11,246
The court laid out the method. Let's walk
through it.

47
00:03:11,796 --> 00:03:13,098
Step one. Companies.

48
00:03:13,098 --> 00:03:18,370
According to state media, investigators
counted more than a thousand companies in

49
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:23,707
the Van Thinh Phat network. Many of them
existed mainly on paper. Ghost companies,

50
00:03:23,707 --> 00:03:27,743
with people listed as directors who often
didn't run anything.

51
00:03:28,293 --> 00:03:29,570
Step two. Loans.

52
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:35,714
Those companies applied to SCB for loans.
Fake applications, the court found,

53
00:03:35,714 --> 00:03:40,182
approved by managers who knew where the
money was going.

54
00:03:40,182 --> 00:03:46,566
Between 2018 and 2022 alone, the court
counted 916 such loan applications, worth

55
00:03:46,566 --> 00:03:48,561
around 545 trillion dong.

56
00:03:49,111 --> 00:03:50,669
Step three. Collateral.

57
00:03:50,669 --> 00:03:55,953
Every loan needs security. According to
the court, appraisal firms colluded to

58
00:03:55,953 --> 00:04:00,899
inflate the value of the assets pledged,
so the paperwork looked covered.

59
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:03,494
Step four. The money moves on.

60
00:04:03,494 --> 00:04:08,742
Once disbursed, the loan money was
shuffled between accounts, used to pay off

61
00:04:08,742 --> 00:04:13,718
older loans, poured into Van Thinh Phat's
projects, or taken out in cash.

62
00:04:13,968 --> 00:04:19,780
Each step, on its own, looked like
ordinary banking. A loan. A valuation. A

63
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:25,670
transfer. Only together did they form a
pipe that ran in one direction: out.

64
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:29,340
And here's where the driver comes in.

65
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:36,002
According to prosecutors, from February
2019 to 2022, Lan's driver carried cash

66
00:04:36,002 --> 00:04:43,086
from SCB to her company's headquarters and
to her home. His notebook added up to 108

67
00:04:43,086 --> 00:04:46,796
trillion dong, plus 14.7 million US
dollars.

68
00:04:47,346 --> 00:04:52,885
Even in Vietnam's largest banknote, that
is more than two hundred million notes.

69
00:04:53,435 --> 00:05:00,415
Over ten years, the court said, SCB made
more than 2,500 loans into Lan's network.

70
00:05:00,415 --> 00:05:07,054
It found that she had embezzled 304
trillion dong. About 12.5 billion dollars.

71
00:05:07,054 --> 00:05:13,608
International media noted that was close
to three percent of Vietnam's entire

72
00:05:13,608 --> 00:05:14,970
economy in 2022.

73
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:19,527
A hole that big should be visible from the
outside.

74
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:23,938
Banks in Vietnam are inspected by the
State Bank, the central bank.

75
00:05:23,938 --> 00:05:25,386
And SCB was inspected.

76
00:05:25,936 --> 00:05:31,050
According to the court, the bank's general
director paid the head of a central-bank

77
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:34,378
inspection team 5.2 million dollars, in
four payments.

78
00:05:34,378 --> 00:05:38,814
International reporting from the trial
described some of that cash being

79
00:05:38,814 --> 00:05:40,601
delivered in styrofoam boxes.

80
00:05:40,851 --> 00:05:46,271
In return, the court found, the inspection
findings were softened. SCB's real

81
00:05:46,271 --> 00:05:47,960
condition stayed hidden.

82
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:53,802
So the bank kept looking healthy on paper.
Depositors kept depositing. And the hole

83
00:05:53,802 --> 00:05:54,717
kept growing.

84
00:05:55,267 --> 00:06:00,893
The inspection chief was sentenced to life
in prison. Her appeal was rejected.

85
00:06:00,893 --> 00:06:06,879
She was one of fifteen former central-bank
officials who stood trial alongside Lan,

86
00:06:06,879 --> 00:06:12,721
along with officials from the Government
Inspectorate and the State Audit Office.

87
00:06:13,721 --> 00:06:15,350
Think about what that means.

88
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:20,236
The people whose job was to check the bank
were, according to the court, part of how

89
00:06:20,236 --> 00:06:21,748
the bank stayed unchecked.

90
00:06:22,948 --> 00:06:29,153
From 2018, the court found, Lan's group
tapped a second source of cash: ordinary

91
00:06:29,153 --> 00:06:29,696
savers.

92
00:06:30,246 --> 00:06:35,282
Four companies linked to Van Thinh Phat
issued 25 batches of corporate bonds

93
00:06:35,282 --> 00:06:36,739
between 2018 and 2020.

94
00:06:36,739 --> 00:06:42,173
The court found these were fake bonds, and
the money raised was never used for the

95
00:06:42,173 --> 00:06:43,233
purposes stated.

96
00:06:43,483 --> 00:06:47,187
They were sold through a securities firm
and SCB's own branches.

97
00:06:47,437 --> 00:06:52,651
To a saver, the difference between a
deposit and a bond can look like a few

98
00:06:52,651 --> 00:06:58,282
lines of small print. A deposit is a claim
on the bank, backed, up to a limit, by

99
00:06:58,282 --> 00:07:03,844
deposit insurance. A corporate bond is a
loan to a company. If the company can't

100
00:07:03,844 --> 00:07:05,304
pay, you can lose it.

101
00:07:05,854 --> 00:07:10,593
Most of the buyers were SCB depositors.
According to state media, bank staff

102
00:07:10,593 --> 00:07:14,272
reassured them the bonds were safe, like a
savings account.

103
00:07:14,522 --> 00:07:18,827
State media also reported that the bank's
general director held training sessions

104
00:07:18,827 --> 00:07:21,431
for thousands of sales staff on how to
sell them.

105
00:07:21,981 --> 00:07:28,686
The court counted 35,824 victims and more
than 30 trillion dong taken, about 1.2

106
00:07:28,686 --> 00:07:30,026
billion dollars.

107
00:07:30,026 --> 00:07:36,647
Where did it go? Repaying bank loans.
Paying interest on older bonds. Projects.

108
00:07:36,647 --> 00:07:41,927
Transfers abroad. And, the court said,
Lan's personal spending.

109
00:07:43,127 --> 00:07:45,937
In October 2022, it all came apart.

110
00:07:45,937 --> 00:07:48,346
Police arrested Truong My Lan.

111
00:07:48,896 --> 00:07:54,101
Within days, worried depositors crowded
SCB branches to pull out their savings.

112
00:07:54,101 --> 00:07:59,372
For many families, SCB was simply the bank
down the street. They had no idea who

113
00:07:59,372 --> 00:08:00,756
really controlled it.

114
00:08:01,006 --> 00:08:06,590
The State Bank placed SCB under special
control and sent in managers from the big

115
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:07,831
state-owned banks.

116
00:08:08,381 --> 00:08:12,347
To keep the bank alive, the central bank
kept lending to it.

117
00:08:12,347 --> 00:08:17,370
By February 2025, Reuters reported, the
central bank had lent SCB about 25.6

118
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:18,428
billion dollars.

119
00:08:18,428 --> 00:08:23,584
And the bondholders discovered that the
companies behind their bonds could not

120
00:08:23,584 --> 00:08:23,848
pay.

121
00:08:24,098 --> 00:08:28,969
According to state media, they filed
complaints with police and petitioned the

122
00:08:28,969 --> 00:08:31,529
authorities, asking for their money back.

123
00:08:31,529 --> 00:08:36,649
In effect, central-bank money was keeping
a private bank alive, because letting it

124
00:08:36,649 --> 00:08:39,959
fail risked spreading panic through the
whole system.

125
00:08:41,159 --> 00:08:46,065
On March 5, 2024, the trial opened at the
Ho Chi Minh City People's Court.

126
00:08:46,065 --> 00:08:51,038
It was part of the Communist Party's
long-running anti-corruption campaign,

127
00:08:51,038 --> 00:08:53,093
known as the "blazing furnace".

128
00:08:53,643 --> 00:09:00,606
Eighty-six defendants. About 2,700 people
summoned as witnesses. Around 200 lawyers.

129
00:09:00,606 --> 00:09:06,492
And, according to the BBC, 104 boxes of
case files weighing six tonnes.

130
00:09:06,492 --> 00:09:13,290
Lan denied embezzling. She said she had
only a small stake in the bank, and blamed

131
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:14,699
her subordinates.

132
00:09:14,949 --> 00:09:19,530
The court rejected that. It said she had
orchestrated a sophisticated criminal

133
00:09:19,530 --> 00:09:20,176
enterprise.

134
00:09:20,726 --> 00:09:24,343
On April 11, 2024, the court gave its
verdict.

135
00:09:24,893 --> 00:09:31,148
Truong My Lan: guilty of embezzlement,
bribery, and violating banking rules.

136
00:09:31,148 --> 00:09:32,795
The sentence: death.

137
00:09:32,795 --> 00:09:39,050
The court ordered her to pay back around
674 trillion dong, about 27 billion

138
00:09:39,050 --> 00:09:40,367
dollars, to SCB.

139
00:09:40,367 --> 00:09:45,717
It said there was little chance the money
could all be recovered.

140
00:09:46,267 --> 00:09:51,680
Her husband got nine years. Her niece, who
ran Van Thinh Phat, got seventeen.

141
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:57,024
Four defendants were sentenced to life:
two former chairmen of the bank, its

142
00:09:57,024 --> 00:10:01,453
former general director, and the
central-bank inspection chief.

143
00:10:01,453 --> 00:10:04,054
Every one of the 86 was found guilty.

144
00:10:05,254 --> 00:10:11,405
In the autumn of 2024, Lan was back in the
same court, this time for the bonds.

145
00:10:11,405 --> 00:10:17,400
On October 17, she was found guilty of
fraud, money laundering, and illegally

146
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:19,580
moving money across borders.

147
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:26,258
The court found she had laundered more
than 445 trillion dong, and illegally

148
00:10:26,258 --> 00:10:33,194
moved more than 4.5 billion dollars across
Vietnam's borders. She was sentenced to

149
00:10:33,194 --> 00:10:33,617
life.

150
00:10:34,167 --> 00:10:38,474
In December 2024, an appeals court upheld
her death sentence.

151
00:10:38,474 --> 00:10:44,193
But under Vietnamese law, it noted, she
could avoid execution if she paid back at

152
00:10:44,193 --> 00:10:47,229
least three-quarters of what she had
taken.

153
00:10:47,479 --> 00:10:52,899
International media called it a race
against time: her life seemed to depend on

154
00:10:52,899 --> 00:10:55,231
how fast her empire could be sold.

155
00:10:55,481 --> 00:11:00,852
In April 2025, ruling on her appeal in the
bond case, the court cut her fraud

156
00:11:00,852 --> 00:11:06,222
sentence from life to twenty years, after
money began to be recovered for the

157
00:11:06,222 --> 00:11:07,059
bondholders.

158
00:11:08,059 --> 00:11:10,091
Then the law itself changed.

159
00:11:10,091 --> 00:11:15,824
In June 2025, Vietnam's National Assembly
abolished the death penalty for eight

160
00:11:15,824 --> 00:11:18,074
crimes, including embezzlement.

161
00:11:18,324 --> 00:11:23,248
Death sentences already handed down for
those crimes would not be carried out.

162
00:11:23,248 --> 00:11:28,108
Instead, the head of the Supreme People's
Court would convert them to life in

163
00:11:28,108 --> 00:11:28,550
prison.

164
00:11:28,550 --> 00:11:32,022
Her lawyer told AFP that Truong My Lan
would be spared.

165
00:11:33,222 --> 00:11:37,730
For the victims, the question was never
her sentence. It was their money.

166
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:44,257
Investigators had frozen more than 1,200
properties linked to her, and hundreds of

167
00:11:44,257 --> 00:11:48,777
millions of SCB shares held in her name or
her proxies' names.

168
00:11:48,777 --> 00:11:53,515
Ho Chi Minh City's civil judgment
enforcement office began paying

169
00:11:53,515 --> 00:11:55,337
bondholders in June 2025.

170
00:11:55,587 --> 00:12:02,122
By May 2026, according to the Vietnamese
government's news portal, nine rounds had

171
00:12:02,122 --> 00:12:08,656
paid out about 12 trillion dong, roughly
40 percent of what was owed, to more than

172
00:12:08,656 --> 00:12:10,011
42,000 creditors.

173
00:12:10,261 --> 00:12:15,897
A tenth payment followed in July 2026. It
was worth about one percent of what was

174
00:12:15,897 --> 00:12:16,245
owed.

175
00:12:16,245 --> 00:12:21,881
For a retiree who put their savings into a
bond they believed was a deposit, that

176
00:12:21,881 --> 00:12:25,639
means waiting, year after year, for a
slice at a time.

177
00:12:26,189 --> 00:12:31,119
Her possessions are being sold. Two
designer handbags. A Maybach. A yacht

178
00:12:31,119 --> 00:12:34,225
that, after five auctions, still had no
buyer.

179
00:12:34,225 --> 00:12:39,087
She had asked the court to let her family
keep the handbags. It refused.

180
00:12:39,637 --> 00:12:42,886
But the bondholders are only part of the
bill.

181
00:12:42,886 --> 00:12:48,608
The 27 billion dollars owed to SCB is on
another scale entirely. The court itself

182
00:12:48,608 --> 00:12:51,646
warned that much of it may never come
back.

183
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:58,674
And SCB? As of August 2026, state media
reported, it was still under special

184
00:12:58,674 --> 00:13:01,349
control, and closing branches.

185
00:13:02,549 --> 00:13:05,617
Strip away the numbers, and the shape is
simple.

186
00:13:05,617 --> 00:13:09,580
One. The lender and the borrower are
secretly the same person.

187
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,671
Two. The loans hide behind companies that
exist mostly on paper.

188
00:13:13,671 --> 00:13:17,698
Three. The collateral is inflated, so
everything looks covered.

189
00:13:17,948 --> 00:13:22,310
Four. The people who are supposed to
check, don't. Or are paid not to.

190
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:27,171
And five. When the hole grows, it gets
filled with money from ordinary savers,

191
00:13:27,171 --> 00:13:29,975
sold something risky as if it were a
deposit.

192
00:13:30,975 --> 00:13:36,989
In this case, one detail made it worse.
The bonds were sold inside the bank, by

193
00:13:36,989 --> 00:13:42,698
people wearing the bank's uniform. The
trust people had in the bank was the

194
00:13:42,698 --> 00:13:43,307
product.

195
00:13:43,307 --> 00:13:49,092
This is not unique to Vietnam. Insider
lending has broken banks all over the

196
00:13:49,092 --> 00:13:49,549
world.

197
00:13:49,799 --> 00:13:54,372
If someone at a bank counter offers you a
product with a better rate than a deposit,

198
00:13:54,372 --> 00:13:57,257
ask one question: who is actually
borrowing my money?

199
00:13:58,457 --> 00:14:03,472
She began at a market stall. She ended
with a court bill bigger than most

200
00:14:03,472 --> 00:14:05,121
companies will ever see.

201
00:14:05,121 --> 00:14:10,960
Her empire was built on property. But what
it really ran on was other people's trust.

202
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:14,326
And somewhere in between, a bank became a
wallet.

203
00:14:15,326 --> 00:14:21,305
Next time: China. An online platform that
promised safety, backed by contracts and

204
00:14:21,305 --> 00:14:25,170
celebrity ads… and 900,000 investors who
believed it.

205
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,340
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

206
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:31,103
And tell me in the comments: would you
know if your bank was selling you

207
00:14:31,103 --> 00:14:32,776
something that wasn't a deposit?

